# $package_title

A product on the [Synapse SaaS Framework](https://github.com/allandanos/synapse-saas):
auth, tenancy, RBAC, plans, entitlements, usage metering, billing, webhooks
and the console come from the package; this repository holds only the
product — a Projects CRUD to start from.

```bash
uv sync                                   # installs synapse-saas + this package
docker compose up -d postgres redis        # or point SYNAPSE_DATABASE_URL anywhere
cp .env.example .env
make migrate                              # framework migrations + this product's branch
make seed                                 # permissions, system roles, plan catalog
make dev                                  # http://localhost:8000/docs
make test
```

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `src/$package/models.py` | `Project(TenantMixin, Base)` — one line of tenancy |
| `src/$package/router.py` | CRUD: permission-checked, plan-limited (`projects` gauge), audited |
| `src/$package/app.py` | `create_product_app()` = framework `create_app()` + your routers |
| `src/$package/worker.py` | your cron jobs, on the framework's arq worker |
| `migrations/` | an Alembic **branch** (`$package`) that depends on the framework head; run via `python -m $package.migrate` |
| `config/plans.yaml` | your pricing (start from the framework's default catalog) |
| `tests/` | run on the framework's public pytest plugin |

## Upgrading the framework

Bump `synapse-saas` in `pyproject.toml`, `uv sync`, `make migrate`. Your
migrations never touch framework tables; the framework's never touch yours.
